Z||000001||ka4nkf||05-16-2001||10:18 PM||||I don't think this fan is necessary, after all they did discontinue it in the 88'. I removed the cooling tubes and disconected the fan motor. I have on order from Rodney Dickman a new fan switch that comes on at 210 and off at 200. this should be ideal, and keep the heat down. I think the coolant temp. in these cars is so high , that is one reason we have heater core problems because the coolant reaches 235 and the solder gives away. anyway I will find out after I install the new fan switch.||||reg||1
